Brave Ones!

Have you been waiting for a new update? Well, here it is! So, put on your armor, grab your best weapons, and set off on new adventures! And we’ll tell you what awaits you right now.

New platform release — macOS

We're pleased to announce our game's release on the macOS platform. Mac users will now be able to dive into the exciting world of Singoru, full of battles, adventures, and loyal allies!

The Braves has been carefully optimized for macOS to provide a smooth and immersive gameplay experience. The new version will also support all the features available on other platforms.

The game is already available for download on Steam. Don't miss this opportunity to become a part of The Braves' world and experience all of its incredible adventures right on your Mac!

Authorization 101XP

Now you can use authorization via 101XP, which opens the doors to new platforms. A new era is coming soon when you will be able to enjoy the game on different platforms, and logging in via 101XP will be the first step towards this. 

The authorization process is incredibly simple: just go to the settings menu in the upper-left corner of the screen and click on the “101XP Account" button. Then follow the instructions and keep playing for fun!

Please note that at the moment, it is only possible to link your Steam progress with your 101XP account. We will announce the release of the game on other platforms separately!

Gift Marathon: Deity Incarnate

The new Gift Marathon, Deity Incarnate, has already begun! Can you feel the heavy steps of the approaching God of War? Time to claim gifts by logging into the game — treat yourself and your heroes during the next 14 days! 

Don't forget that you can also grab a Premium Ticket to receive even more gifts, including a unique Guan Yu skin, the hero himself, and his Legendary weapon!

New Portals Opening

Can you feel the cold breath emanating from the portal? Waves of ether guide unfamiliar heroes to Singoru, and the newcomers know exactly how to cool their enemies' ardor down! With that said, let's welcome the Polar Night and Cold Mystery Portals!
3 new unique heroes await you in the Polar Night Portal. What exactly can they do, and how will the trio surprise you? Time to find out!
Antiope
Legendary Support Heroine Deep within the forest, where trees whisper under the light of the cold stars, there dwelt a girl named Antiope. One day, strange creatures tried to break the privacy of her quiet life. Thus, she became a relentless protector, ready to defend her sacred domain. After all, the astral power at her command could only be matched by Antiope's stalwart resolve. Now, take a look at what she can do:
Legendary Rarity:

 50% chance to inflict triple damage with Stone Shrapnel and its evolutions;
 Explosive Reaction. Stone Shrapnel projectiles explode at the end of their flight, dealing double the skill damage;
 -40% cooldown time for Stone Shrapnel and its evolutions;
 +1 to Stone Shrapnel’s Boulder evolution level;
 -15% movement speed;
 +7.5% movement speed for every Earth Skill, equipped during the match.
 Starry Night Reflection. Upon picking ingredients up, summons the Starry Night Reflection, which damages and lowers the enemies' attack power;
 Starburst. Upon picking misc items up, summons a Starburst that damages all on-screen foes;
 Forest Wisdom. Grants a chance to receive a 15% dodge rate buff for 5 sec. when collecting EXP. Can activate once every 10 sec.

Mythic Rarity:

 Wrath of the Stars. Whenever you land a hit with an Earth skill, there's a chance to inflict the damage-over-time Wrath of the Stars debuff on the enemy.

Guan Yu
Legendary Support Hero. Wrapped in a radiant halo, the God of War descends onto the battlefield to instill fear and awe in the hearts of his enemies. Armed with the right weapon, he's ready to rush into the thick of things! This hero's every move is capable of altering the course of battle, bringing victory to those who fight under his banner... But while we're waiting for the skirmish to start, let's take a look at Guan Yu's formidable abilities:
Legendary Rarity:

 Upon receiving damage, Guan Yu has a chance to fall into the state of Righteous Indignation for 15 sec., losing his unique bonuses to armor, HP regeneration, and movement speed. Instead, the God of War receives equally powerful offensive capabilities, including a chance to inflict x5 damage with Devastating Blow and its evolutions, reduced skill cooldown, and boosted projective speed. The effect can be triggered every 35 sec.;
 Upon receiving damage, Guan Yu also has a chance to summon a single Pikeman that will damage nearby enemies. This effect can be triggered once every 2 sec.;
 Any foe that has landed a hit on Guan Yu with a skill of their own receives a Divine Mark, which boosts their damage for 5 sec.;
 When damaging an enemy with the Divine Mark, Guan Yu summon a Pikeman that will damage nearby enemies. This effect can be triggered once every 2 sec.;
 +35% armor;
 -2 sec. off Hastened Metabolism's cooldown time;
 +15% movement speed;
 +2 revivals;
 When revived, Guan Yu enters the Battle Rage state for 5 sec., gaining increased enemy knock back to quickly clear the surrounding area;
 +1 Hastened Metabolism skill level at the start of the match.

Mythic Rarity:

 Upon receiving damage, Guan Yu has a chance to fall into the state of Righteous Indignation for 15 sec. receiving powerful offensive capabilities: a chance to inflict x5 damage with Devastating Blow and its evolutions, reduced skill cooldown, and boosted projective speed. The effect can be triggered every 35 sec.

Skalda
Epic Defensive Heroine. Skalda originated in the cold northern heights where the harsh winds sharpened her crystal body. In those frozen lands, perpetually covered in snow and ice, she has learned to discern the voices of the mountains and understand the speech of the storm. Now, let's take a closer look at what this heroine can do:
Epic Rarity:

 Seismic Wave. Fires a seismic wave in the selected direction once every 7 sec. Upon colliding with an enemy, the wave deals damage and leaves an uplift behind, which also wounds and slows opponents down;
 30% chance to double activate Surveyor and its evolutions;
 +4 projectiles for Surveyor and its evolutions;
 -25% damage to Surveyor and its evolutions;
 +20% Earth skills' AoE size;
 -20% Earth skills' cooldown time;
 Upon dealing Earth skill damage, has a chance to lower the enemy's attack power by 50% for the next 5 sec.

Legendary Rarity:

 +0.5% armor for every 1% of missing HP;
 0.5% chance to restore 1% HP when dealing Earth skill damage;

Mythic Rarity:

 30% chance to double activate Surveyor and its evolutions.


3 new unique weapons await you in the Cold Mystery Portal, namely:

Star Catcher.
Legendary Stone Thrower. Grants the Stone Shrapnel skill when equipped.

 +30% Stone Shrapnel damage on Uncommon Rarity;
 +5% universal skill damage on Rare Rarity;
 +1 Stone Shrapnel skill level at the start of the match on Epic Rarity;
 +50% Stone Shrapnel size on Legendary Rarity;
 +1 Boulder evolution level on Mythic Rarity.


Jade Dragon. 
Legendary Giant Slayer. Grants the Devastating Blow skill when equipped.

 +30% Devastating Blow damage on Uncommon Rarity;
 +5% universal skill damage on Rare Rarity;
 +1 Devastating Blow skill level at the start of the match on Epic Rarity;
 +350% Devastating Blow knockback force on Legendary Rarity;
 +1 Compass of Pain evolution level on Mythic Rarity.


Ice Legacy. 
Legendary Cadastral Registry. Grants the Surveyor skill when equipped.

 +30% Surveyor damage on Uncommon Rarity;
 +5% universal skill damage on Rare Rarity;
 +1 Surveyor skill level at the start of the match on Epic Rarity;
 +5%% Surveyor skill damage for every 10 level gained during the same match on Legendary Rarity;
 +1 Earthquake evolution level on Mythic Rarity.

New Hero Skins

 Our heroes continue to try on new outfits. We're proud to present some of the most notable additions:
 Guan Dy: +2.5% attack power for every 10 levels gained in the same match (only obtainable from the premium Gift Marathon: Deity Incarnate);
 Fireworks Master Tieme: bombs deal 24% more damage;
 Dancing Dragon Nailus: +15.5% damage dealt with the 4th and subsequent projectiles after each skill activation;
 Yin-Yang Visconti: 5.5% chance to deal double damage;
 Tempesta Crane: +5% dodge rate;
 Night Mistress Antiope: +11% EXP drop rate from defeated enemies;
 Martial Arts Master Bastet: 2.75% chance to deal triple damage.
 You can already find most of these at the Tavern and purchase them with Gems or Transformation Masks.


New Achievements

New heroes mean new achievements! For those who like to deck out their profiles both in-game and on Steam, we've prepared 3 new achievements related to Antiope, Skalda, and Guan Yu.

Bug fixes:


 Aurora: Fixed the hero's skill knockback specialization bonus — it'll now work correctly and provide a 125% increase. Previously, this perk would multiply the knockback force by 1.25 regardless of skill-specific values.

