Brave Ones!

Christmas and New Year's are fast approaching, and we've prepared a new update that will bring even more holiday spirit to Singoru. So, here's what awaits you:

It is important to note that the update will tentatively be installed at 00:00 UTC.

New Event: Frosty Harvest
A terrible chill is coming from the north, and ominous figures are marching alongside it, which clearly means trouble. The land is growing cold, putting the already scarce crops at risk, and only the Bravest of the Brave can avert the approaching catastrophe!

Hurry up and check the new mode at the Forest location. Singoru and its inhabitants need your aid like never before!

New Mode: Frosty Harvest. Go to the Forest location under the "To Battle!" tab and choose Frost Harvest from the list of modes. It's only available in the Forest and comes with 5 difficulty levels. Pick the difficulty that suits you and defeat the Frost Reaper on your own terms!
New Enemy: Frost Reaper. An enigmatic fiend that has come from beyond the Mountainous Ridge, leading other monsters and unnatural cold to devour the fertile lands. This being knows no pain or pity but worst of all—no defeat. Can you find its weak spot and vanquish this new scourge?
New Mechanic: Invulnerable Opponent.  The Frost Reaper is protected by a shield of impenetrable cold, so no attack will cause it any harm, even if you recruit hellfire itself. To defeat this powerful foe, one needs to find something on the battlefield that can lower or temporarily limit its defenses.
New Special Point of Interest: Frost Pylon. Search the Forest location in the Frost Harvest mode, and you will find special points of interest. These are the sources of the Frost Reaper's power, and destroying them will deactivate its shield of cold, so that you can strike a decisive blow.
Event Token: Festive Bells. A symbol of the winter holidays, obtained by defeating the Frost Reaper. Nobody knows why the monster collected these in the first place, but you can bring them to the Market and exchange them for valuable rewards.
Event Currency: Festive Mask. Some of the heroes have received new skins at the Tavern. You can purchase them with Gems or Festive Masks.
Event Rewards: 
- During the event's first stage, you can try your luck at the Market and randomly exchange Event Tokens for one of the following rewards:
New Winter Lord armor set pieces;

 Academy Runes;
 Prism Fragments;
 Ether Prisms;
 Eternity Prisms;
 Gold Coins;
 Building materials;
 Heroic Manga;
 Blueprints;
 Festive Masks.


New Hero Skins
We've recently witnessed the entire village's wonderful transformation: the spirit of winter holidays is in the air, and no one can resist their call. Thus, some of the characters decided that it was high time to update their wardrobe by preparing new costumes to celebrate the occasion:

 Truffaldino (Obtained from the Festive Miracle Premium Gift Marathon);
 Sister Remoria (Obtained from the  New Year's Premium Gift Marathon);
 Jack;
 Risha;
 Limuru;
 Zena;
 Sobek;
 Elusive Ice;
 Dancing Flame.

Gift Marathon: Festive Miracle and New Year's Gifts
Festive Miracle: The new Gift Marathon has already started! Do you feel the holiday spirit in the air? Collect gifts by logging in and treat yourself as well as your heroes during the next 7 days!
New Year's Gifts: Another Gift Marathon is set to begin on December 31, timed to coincide with the New Year's Eve! It'll last for as long as 28 days, almost until the very end of January.
A reminder that you can grab Premium Tickets for both marathons to receive even more gifts, including unique skins for Sister Remoria and Truffaldino, as well as Gemstones, Festive Masks, new armor sets, wepons and more!

New Armor Set: Winter Lord
It's said that Winter Lords were ancient guardians, tasked with preventing the monsters that dwell in the northern wastelands from event crossing the Mountainous Ridge. It's a mystery what became of them, but you can now take up the mantle of a Winter Lord yourself and stand up for the innocent people of the warm southern lands! And while you're at it, why not claim this set of armor at the Market as a random reward for opening chests with Festive Bells? What are the advantages of the Winter Lord set, you ask? Well, let's take a closer look:

Winter Lord Headwear:

 +5% Max HP on Uncommon Rarity;
 +15% Max HP on Rare Rarity;
 +5 sec. of invulnerability upon being revived on Epic Rarity;
 +1 revival during a match on Legendary Rarity;
 -23% cooldown time for all Water Skills and their evolutions on Mythic Rarity.

Winter Lord Boots:

 +5% Max HP on Uncommon Rarity;
 +15% Max HP on Rare Rarity;
 +125% EXP pick-up radius on Epic Rarity;
 +7,25 movement speed on Legendary Rarity;
 +30% chance to Double Activate all Water Skills on Mythic Rarity.

Winter Lord Armor:

 +5% Max HP on Uncommon Rarity;
 +15% Max HP on Rare Rarity;
 -9% incoming damage on Epic Rarity;
 Increased Accelerated Metabolism activation rate on Legendary Rarity;
 -13% incoming damage on Mythic Rarity.

Winter Lord Mittens:

 +5% Max HP on Uncommon Rarity;
 +15% Max HP on Rare Rarity;
 +10% chance to deal х3 damage with all Water Skills on Epic Rarity;
 +105% skill knockback force on Legendary Rarity;
 +10% chance to deal х4 damage with all Water Skills on Mythic Rarity.

Winter Lord Ring:

 +5% Max HP on Uncommon Rarity;
 +15% Max HP on Rare Rarity;
 -10% movement speed for 1 sec. to enemies upon hitting them with a skill on Epic Rarity;
 +10% chance to recover 10% HP upon receiving damage on Legendary Rarity;
 +0.75% chance to heal by 1% Max HP when dealing damage with a water skill on Mythic Rarity.

And don't forget that, if you collect and equip the entire Winter Lord set, you will receive another ability: When you pick up a cure, it activates a frost shield that gives you invulnerability for 6 sec. This ability has a roll time of 16 sec.
